# GLM-5.3-Flash W4A16 on 4 CUDA GPUs (sm_80 Ampere patches)
# Copy to .env and edit. ./start.sh does this for you on first run.
# A prefix env assignment overrides this file for every key, including an
# explicit empty (KEY= ./start.sh):   MAX_LEN=131072 ./start.sh restart

# --- engine pin --------------------------------------------------------
# The vLLM fork and the commit it is pinned to. Left commented so a `git pull`
# of this repo can move the pin; ./start.sh reinstalls when it changes.
# Uncomment to freeze the engine, or roll back for one run with
#   VLLM_COMMIT=<older sha> ./start.sh update
# TODO(1.3.0 release): the merged, validated commit replaces ff4750db5d here.
# VLLM_COMMIT=ff4750db5d
# VLLM_REPO=https://github.com/Morrowmake/vllm-cmp170hx.git
# VLLM_BRANCH=ampere-glm53

# --- paths -------------------------------------------------------------
# All default to directories inside this repo.
# VENV=./venv
# VLLM_SRC=./vllm-src
# MODELS_DIR=./models
# MODEL=./models/GLM-5.3-Flash-W4A16-MTP
# DFLASH_MODEL=./models/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2
# CUDA toolkit root. Triton and TileLang JIT against it at runtime.
CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-13.3

# --- weights -----------------------------------------------------------
TARGET_REPO=canada-quant/GLM-5.3-Flash-W4A16-MTP
DRAFTER_REPO=incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2
# Unauthenticated Hub downloads are rate limited; a token is faster.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx
# REFRESH_WEIGHTS=1 re-fetches even when the files are already there.

# --- API ---------------------------------------------------------------
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=8000
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=glm-5.3-flash
# Parsers for GLM-5.3's reasoning blocks and tool calls.
REASONING_PARSER=glm47
TOOL_PARSER=glm47

# --- layout ------------------------------------------------------------
# tp4 (default) -- tensor-parallel 4. Fastest per request: one or two
#   interactive agents. Every number in the README's main tables uses it. It
#   assumes PCIe Gen2 x16 links between the cards: tensor parallelism moves
#   about 9.4 MB per layer during prefill and roughly 100 small collectives
#   per decode step, so on stock x4 links it is bus-bound and far slower than
#   the published figures.
# pp4 -- pipeline-parallel 4. EXPERIMENTAL in this release. For many parallel
#   agents, long prefills, more KV, and boards with narrow links. Also DFlash2.
# LAYOUT, when set, wins over PP/TP. Left commented so serve.sh picks tp4.
# LAYOUT=tp4
# Raw layout knobs, used only when LAYOUT is unset. PP * TP must equal 4.
# PP=1
# TP=4
# Layer split under PP only. Empty uses the balanced default for the mode.
# VLLM_PP_LAYER_PARTITION=

# --- engine sizing -----------------------------------------------------
# Context ceiling. On engine ff4750db5d with 1,152-token prefill chunks, 262144
# gave a 1,160,192-token KV pool at GPU_UTIL 0.95, 4.43x concurrency at full
# context; with this release's defaults: PENDING. Raising it lowers that.
MAX_LEN=262144
# Concurrent sequences.
MAX_SEQS=8
# Batched tokens per scheduler step; this sets the prefill chunk size:
# chunk = floor((MAX_BATCHED - SPEC_N) / 1152) x 1152. Left commented so
# serve.sh picks it per layout: 3460 under tp4 (3,456-token chunks, +2.4% to
# +3.6% cold prefill against 2,304-token chunks for about 35,600 fewer KV
# tokens), 2312 under pp4. 2048 gives 1.2.0's 1,152-token chunks.
# MAX_BATCHED=3460
# Fraction of each GPU vLLM may use. 0.95 is what we run; 0.97 was too tight.
GPU_UTIL=0.95

# --- speculative decoding ----------------------------------------------
# dflash = the DFlash2 drafter (needs DRAFTER_REPO downloaded)
# mtp    = the MTP head inside the target checkpoint
# none   = no speculation
# dflash under both layouts. Uncomment to force another.
# SPEC_MODE=dflash
# Draft tokens per step. k=3 is what the README numbers use.
SPEC_N=3

# --- prefill -----------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream's UNCONDITIONAL long-prefill chunk cap. LEAVE IT 0. It cost -15.3%
# prefill and +16.5% TTFT@23K here, and it silently disables the prefill
# overlap and the prefill kernels by dropping chunks below their gates.
PREFILL_CAP=0
# Decode-aware chunking: the cap that only applies while something is decoding.
# This is the one you want. 0 turns it off.
FAIR_PREFILL=1
FAIR_CHUNK=384
FAIR_PARTIAL=2

# --- sm_80 feature flags (kill switches) -------------------------------
# All seven are OFF by default in the engine code; serve.sh is the only thing
# that turns them on, so each is a one-variable kill switch. Set one to 0 and
# restart — no rebuild, no revert.
#
# If output quality is ever in question, turn VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_KERNELS off
# first: it owns the small exactness movement we measured (GSM8K 1.000 ->
# 0.980 at n=50 when the seven were merged).
#
# Three of them only mean something with TP>1, so they are left commented
# and serve.sh sets them per layout (1 under tp4, 0 or unset under pp4).
# Uncomment one only to force it.
#
# TP prefill comm/compute overlap (TP>1 only).
# VLLM_GLM5_PREFILL_OVERLAP=1
VLLM_GLM5_PREFILL_OVERLAP_SPLITS=2
# sm_80 prefill kernels: mHC pre-norm projection + sparse-MLA DSA attention.
VLLM_GLM5_PREFILL_KERNELS=1
# Chunk-size gate for those kernels. 384, not the code default 512, because
# FAIR_CHUNK caps the chunk at 384 while something decodes.
VLLM_GLM5_PREFILL_MIN_TOKENS=384
# Fused eager decode prologue.
VLLM_GLM5_PROLOGUE_FUSE=1
# Batch-sharded logits and sampling (TP>1 only).
# VLLM_GLM5_LOCAL_LOGITS=1
# sm_80 decode kernels: fused mHC post+pre, MoE routing/align, KDA decode.
VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_KERNELS=1
# sm_80 thin-M BF16 GEMM for the linears W4A16 leaves unquantized.
VLLM_GLM5_THIN_GEMM=1
# Host-staged all-reduce for nodes without GPU peer access (TP>1 only; there
# are no TP collectives under pp4).
# VLLM_GLM5_HOST_ALLREDUCE=1
# Submit the MoE shared experts after the routed dispatch so the two overlap
# on the aux stream. Decode only. 0 restores the upstream ordering.
VLLM_GLM5_SHARED_EXPERT_REORDER=1

# TODO(1.3.0 release): five decode changes, tp4 only, OFF until the engine pin
# carries them. serve.sh turns them on under tp4 once it does; each is then a
# kill switch like the ones above. Uncomment only to force one.
# VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_IDX_GLUE=0      # indexer decode glue folded into fewer kernels
# VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_KDA_V2=0        # KDA decode, gate projections fused
# VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_MOE_ROUTE_V2=0  # MoE gate + top-k + align in one kernel
# VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_MHC_V2=0        # mHC decode v2
# VLLM_GLM5_DRAFTER_ROPE_FIT=0     # drafter RoPE cache sized to the context: more KV

# --- optional: PCIe peer-to-peer ---------------------------------------
# Device-memory CustomAllreduce over PCIe peer-to-peer instead of staging
# every collective through the host. OFF here, because peer-to-peer has to be
# available at the driver level first -- `nvidia-smi topo -p2p r` must report
# OK rather than GNS. See "Optional: PCIe peer-to-peer" in the README.
# Worth -5.8% ms/step at one stream and -10.8% at four, cold prefill
# unchanged, and about 21.5k more KV tokens.
VLLM_ALLOW_PCIE_P2P_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE=0
# Which CustomAllreduce kernel. 2stage, because the built-in crossover is
# NVLink-tuned and wrong on Gen2 x16. Inert unless the gate above is 1.
VLLM_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE_ALGO=2stage
# The gate also picks the caching allocator, because CustomAllreduce needs
# legacy CUDA IPC handles that the expandable_segments (VMM) allocator cannot
# provide. Set PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF explicitly only if you mean to override
# that; an explicit value wins over the gate's choice.
# PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=

# --- determinism instruments (available, off) --------------------------
# Both default 0 and are for reproducing exact outputs, not for throughput.
# VLLM_GLM5_TOPK_CANONICAL=0
# VLLM_GLM5_DETERMINISTIC_MOE_ALIGN=0
# Replicated input-embedding table under TP: saves 2 all-reduces per step for
# +0.74 GiB per rank (-6% KV tokens). Off — the KV is worth more here.
VLLM_GLM5_REPLICATED_EMBED=0

# --- multimodal --------------------------------------------------------
# 0 leaves vision and video uncapped, which makes the memory profiler reserve
# for a context-filling video and costs roughly 150k KV tokens.
# 1 bounds both the profiler dummy and real inputs to the values below.
MM_CAP=0
MM_IMAGES=4
MM_FRAMES=32
MM_MAX_PIXELS=1003520

# --- lifecycle ---------------------------------------------------------
# Seconds ./start.sh waits for /health. Weight load plus CUDA-graph capture on
# a 320B MoE is slow.
READY_TIMEOUT=1800
# Seconds ./start.sh stop waits after SIGINT before SIGKILL.
STOP_TIMEOUT=120
# Preflight thresholds. MIN_GPUS should match PP*TP.
MIN_GPUS=4
MIN_GPU_MIB=61440
NEED_DISK_GB=185

# --- build -------------------------------------------------------------
# 0 installs upstream's precompiled extensions (minutes). The patches touch no
# CUDA or C++ source, so they are the same objects you would compile, and they
# already carry sm_80 cubins.
# 1 compiles them yourself: needs the full toolkit, ~60 GB scratch, 1-2 hours.
BUILD_FROM_SOURCE=0
MAX_JOBS=16
# TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=8.0
# Only if torch does not resolve to a CUDA build on your platform. PyPI's
# linux torch 2.13.0 is already the cu130 build.
# TORCH_INDEX_URL=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130

# --- extra -------------------------------------------------------------
# Appended verbatim to the vllm serve command line. A --speculative-config
# here wins and no second one is added.
# EXTRA_ARGS=
